{
  "text": " Before another return deadline slips pass, let your AI help you check what is still eligible. Agents like Muse, Instinct and Dots need your approved access. Find recent purchases. Check return policies and list possible returns with deadlines and source links. Have it include order and delivery dates, item condition fees and anything it cannot verify because a receipt on its own may not establish whether a return is still eligible. Sort the list by deadline so a forgotten purchase does not disappear under another week of email. Then choose the item numbers and ask for a return request draft. Make it show the next step before sending anything, cancelling anything or accepting a charge. For a pair of glasses that means checking the exact policy, preparing the request and showing you the next step. A return label depends on the retailer and the request is not a refund. You still need to check the details and send the item back. The useful part is cutting down all that admin for business software audit upcoming renewals and check the contract before cancelling. I am Hamar Chauhan. Save this prompt and follow for practical AI workflows you can actually use.",
